# Only the paths below need a code owner's approval. Enforcement is the
# "Code owner gate" required status check (.github/workflows/codeowner-gate.yml),
# NOT GitHub's native "Require review from Code Owners" (which does nothing while
# required approvals is 0). The gate reads the path patterns below and:
#   - passes PRs that touch none of them (merge solo);
#   - passes when the PR author is a code owner (CODE_OWNER_LOGINS repo variable);
#   - otherwise blocks until a code owner other than the author approves on the
#     current head commit.
# Keep CODE_OWNER_LOGINS in sync with the @mitch-pro/owners team. The team still
# needs Write access so GitHub honors the reviewer requests these rules create.
# Do not add a catch-all `*` rule: it would gate every PR. See docs/branch-protection.md.
/.github/               @mitch-pro/owners
/tools/deploy.sh        @mitch-pro/owners
/AGENTS.md              @mitch-pro/owners
/rust/crates/mitch-lib/src/auth.rs @mitch-pro/owners

# Build and hosting: what production runs and how traffic reaches it.
/rust/Dockerfile        @mitch-pro/owners
/docker-compose.yml     @mitch-pro/owners
/caddy/                 @mitch-pro/owners
/SECURITY_POSTURE.md    @mitch-pro/owners

# Security gates: the global request gate (CSRF, auth checks), the admin
# passphrase, crypto helpers and the shared admin unlock client.
/rust/crates/mitch-server/src/handler.rs   @mitch-pro/owners
/rust/crates/mitch-lib/src/admin.rs        @mitch-pro/owners
/rust/crates/mitch-lib/src/crypto.rs       @mitch-pro/owners
/webserver/admin-auth.js                   @mitch-pro/owners

# Economy (see the "Economy integrity" rules in AGENTS.md).
/rust/crates/mitch-lib/src/coins.rs                    @mitch-pro/owners
/rust/crates/mitch-lib/src/shop.rs                     @mitch-pro/owners
/rust/crates/mitch-server/src/routes/casino.rs         @mitch-pro/owners
/rust/crates/mitch-server/src/routes/me/cosmetics.rs   @mitch-pro/owners
